  "final": {
    "agentMessage": "According to the California DMV **Service Advisor** result for **“vehicle registration renewal office”**:\n\n**Option 1 – Renew Online (preferred):**\n> *“In most cases, vehicle registration renewal is no longer processed at the DMV office and can be completed quickly and easily online, saving you time and postage.”*\n> - Button: **Renew Online**\n> - If unable to use the simple online application, use the **assisted virtual renewal service**.\n\n**How to renew AT a DMV office instead:**\n\n**Option 2 – DMV Kiosk (in-office, no clerk):**\n> *“DMV Kiosks use touchscreen technology to guide you through renewing your registration. DMV Kiosks are available inside select DMV offices and retail locations during regular business hours.”*\n> - Link: **Find a kiosk near you.**\n\n**Option 6 – In-person renewal when required:**\n> *“There are cases that require renewal in person, such as eligibility, restrictions, etc. In these cases, you may schedule an appointment to renew at the DMV office.”*\n\n**How to save time on the office visit – Option 6 gives 2 choices:**\n\n1. *I am ready to visit the office today.*\n   - Button: **Get in Line Now**\n\n2. *I need an appointment in the future.*\n   - Link: **Make an appointment for registration renewal.**\n\n**Other non-office Options listed:**\n- **Option 3:** Renew by mail to the address on your renewal letter.\n- **Option 4:** Renew by phone at **1-800-777-0133**.\n- **Option 5:** Vehicle registration renewals, duplicate sticker orders, and title transfers can be completed with DMV, or with DMV business partners and auto clubs (partners may charge a fee).\n  - Link: **Find a Business Partner Location**"
  },
